.TH SDL_MinimizeWindow 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_MinimizeWindow \- Request that the window be minimized to an iconic representation.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_MinimizeWindow(SDL_Window *window);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If the window is in a fullscreen state, this request has no direct effect\[char46] It may alter the state the window is returned to when leaving fullscreen\[char46]
.PP
On some windowing systems this request is asynchronous and the new window state may not have been applied immediately upon the return of this function\[char46] If an immediate change is required, call
.BR SDL_SyncWindow ()
to block until the changes have taken effect\[char46]
.PP
When the window state changes, an
.BR SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_MINIMIZED
event will be emitted\[char46] Note that, as this is just a request, the windowing system can deny the state change\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I window
the window to minimize\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_MaximizeWindow (3),
.BR SDL_RestoreWindow (3),
.BR SDL_SyncWindow (3)
